  "answer": {
    "path": "/keno2/fairness",
    "at": "2026-10-12T17:07:28.498Z",
    "body": {
      "version": "canonical",
      "derivation": "block_i = HMAC_SHA256(key = serverSeed, message = clientSeed:nonce:i). Ball i of a round (i = 0 … 9) is bytes 4i..4i+3 of block_0 ‖ block_1 read as a big-endian number u; it is the number at position floor(u × (40 − i) / 2^32) among the numbers not yet drawn, kept in ascending order — the same as floor(float × (40 − i)) with float = Σ byte_j / 256^(j+1), the derivation public Keno calculators use for 40 numbers and 10 draws.",
      "tiles": "Numbers are the tiles 0 to 39 from left to right, top to bottom, shown as 1 to 40.",
      "rules": [
        "pick 1 to 10 numbers and a risk (classic, low, medium or high) before the bet; the ten numbers drawn are fixed by the seed pair and the nonce at the bet",
        "ten different numbers are drawn; the bet pays by how many of the picks are among them, from the paytable of the risk and the number of picks",
        "a payout is the stake × the multiplier, rounded down to the wallet's smallest unit (1e-8) once",
        "a stake whose top prize (every pick drawn) would pay more than the max win above it is refused before the draw",
        "the round settles in the request that places it: there is no round to leave open"
      ],
      "return": "99% at every risk and every number of picks, to within one millionth: each paytable is solved so that Σ P(hits) × multiplier is at most 99/100 and at least 99/100 − 1e-6, with P(hits) hypergeometric on 40 numbers and 10 drawn",
